# An agent asks a verification run that has NOT finished whether it reddened
# one of its own files, and gets an answer.
#
# A full verify takes 50 to 63 minutes on the development box, and 83 to 86% of
# that is two whole-tree Go analyses. Waiting for the published failure index
# (tmp/ze-verify-failures.json) therefore costs an hour to answer a question the
# stage logs already hold: every stage writes tmp/verify/<mode>-<n>/NN-*.log the
# moment it ends, carrying its VERIFY FAILURE GROUP declaration.
#
# The fixture builds a throwaway checkout holding one full-mode run that has
# written 3 of its stage logs, then drives the real `le verify reds` action
# against it. Nothing here touches the real tmp/verify: the native action
# resolves the checkout through ZE_REPO_ROOT, and the fixture replaces it.
#
# The dangerous answer is a green one. `reds` must never render an unfinished
# run as passed, so the untouched path answers "undetermined" with the count of
# stages that have not reported, and a checkout with no run at all answers
# "no-run". Both exit non-zero. Delete either guard
# (internal/le/verify/reds.go, verdictOf) and seq=1 fails.

option=timeout:value=60s




cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture runner/verify-reds-in-flight
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=in-flight-run-ready
expect=stdout:contains=reds-answers-before-the-run-ends
expect=stdout:contains=reds-names-the-reddened-file
expect=stdout:contains=reds-renders-as-json
expect=stdout:contains=reds-refuses-to-answer-with-no-run
